      "byteStart": 1523,
      "byteEnd": 2550,
      "rawText": "Risk: the new records might not reach the existing durable writer or might be returned before flushing. Checked the real task chain at coordinator.js:1420 through reviewAndFix and its noteFixHistory call; runTask finally flushes at :1448, and round completion flushes remaining buffers and drains at :1585-1586. Merge-lane holds and pending-closure producers likewise use noteRecovery/noteLedger. Deferred sweep records queue directly and drain at :1668; Finish closure clears queue directly and drain at :1852. Checked sibling review/seam/check fixer dispatches: each non-null result reaches noteFixHistory. Identical elided Recovery fallbacks retain source/commit facts.\n\nRisk: new durable data could inflate the mechanical reader or be silently lost by the digest. Checked readLedgerPrompt at coordinator.js:2309 and ledger-digest:40-44: the actual reader invokes the modified digest, while oversized lines become source pointers and compact invalid lines reach the explicit decoder gap path. Legacy reducers are unchanged.\n",
